          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Riemannian immersion
            or
            %em isometric immersion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifolds"} Riemannian manifolds
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \hookrightarrow X
            of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            which is also an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
            with respect to their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
          %p
            Similarly, an
            %em isometric embedding
            is an isometric immersion which is also an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding of smooth manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} of the underlying topological spaces
          %p
            The
            %em isometric immersion/embedding problem
            is to find isometric immersions/embeddings of Riemannian manifolds into large-dimensional but flat (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+spaces"}> Euclidean
            ) spaces (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HanHong06"} Han &amp; Hong 2006
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HanLewicka23"} Han &amp; Lewicka 2023
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %p
            Key properties of Riemannian immersion — such as
            %a{:href => "#HarmonicImmersion"} whether
            they are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/harmonic+map"} harmonic
            — are encoded in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor"} tensor
            called their “
            %a{:href => "#SecondFundamentalForm"}> second fundamental form
            ”, which is most immediately expressed in terms of a
            %a{:href => "#AdaptedDarbouxCoframes"} local Darboux coframe field
            adapted to the immerison.
          %p
            %br/
          %p For the following purpose:
          %p
          #LocalCoFrameField.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A (local)
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-frame+field"} co-frame field
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ^
                        %mo ↠
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{X} \twoheadrightarrow X
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-forms"} differential 1-forms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi a
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi dim
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi dR
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = (E^a)_{a=1}^{dim(X)} \,\in\, \Omega^1_{dR}(\widehat{X})
            %p such that on double intersections
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
